Straight-line and about signal disposition, not rooting: it installs SIG_IGN
for SIGPIPE and writes to a reader-closed pipe to prove the write returns EPIPE
instead of the process dying. There is no loop where a root it cares about is
live, so the BIT_GC=stress collector oracle has nothing to verify here — the
value is in the primitive changing the disposition, which the default run
already proves.

This program's OWN code never reaches a safepoint (no loop, confirmed by
inspection), but `BIT_GC=stress` still does not report zero: 5/5 runs measured
`collections=101`, matching stress.bit's own documented scheduler-loop floor
(runtime/sched/workerrun.bit's `Worker.run`). None of those 101 fire at a
back-edge this program emitted, so they still verify nothing about this
program's rooting.
